senses
  entry
    definition "perform an act, usually with a negative connotation"
    examples ("perpetrate a crime" "pull a bank robbery")
    id oewn-02588700-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (perpetrate pull)
  entry
    definition "make a set of changes permanent"
    examples ("We committed the changes to the Git repository")
    id oewn-85001475-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "give entirely to a specific person, activity, or cause"
    examples ("She committed herself to the work of God" "give one's talents to a good cause" "consecrate your life to the church")
    id oewn-00888984-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (give dedicate consecrate devote)
  entry
    definition "cause to be admitted; of persons to an institution"
    examples ("After the second episode, she had to be committed" "he was committed to prison")
    id oewn-02353564-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (institutionalize institutionalise send charge)
  entry
    definition "confer a trust upon"
    examples ("The messenger was entrusted with the general's secret" "I commit my soul to God")
    id oewn-02354208-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (entrust intrust trust confide)
  entry
    definition "make an investment"
    examples ("Put money into bonds")
    id oewn-02275982-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (invest put place)
  entry
    definition "engage in or perform"
    examples ("practice safe sex" "commit a random act of kindness")
    id oewn-02380559-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (practice)
  entry
    definition "transfer to another place so something can be kept or preserved"
    examples ("He committed the poem to memory" "she committed her thoughts to paper")
    id oewn-80672114-v
    partOfSpeech v
